    <div class="jr-prose">

      <h2 id="evidence">Does collagen help brittle nails?</h2>

      <p>
        Possibly, but the case rests on a single small trial, and it is weaker than the marketing
        suggests. The study is worth knowing in detail because nearly every collagen-for-nails claim
        you will read online comes from it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Published in the <em>Journal of Cosmetic Dermatology</em> in 2017, it gave 25 women with
        brittle nails 2.5g a day of a branded bioactive collagen peptide for 24 weeks, then followed
        them for four more weeks off the supplement. Nail growth rate rose by 12%, the frequency of
        broken nails fell by 42%, and 64% of participants were judged to have improved overall.
        Most of the improvement was still visible four weeks after stopping.
      </p>

      <div class="jr-stats">
