      <h2 id="how-long">How long does collagen take to work on nails?</h2>

      <p>
        At least three months to see anything, and six to judge it fairly. That timeline is set by
        how slowly nails grow, not by collagen.
      </p>

      <p>
        A 2010 study of healthy young American adults measured fingernails growing about 3.47mm a
        month and toenails about 1.62mm a month. A whole fingernail takes roughly three to six months
        to replace itself, and a big toenail closer to a year. Any change a supplement makes happens at
        the nail matrix under the cuticle, so you only see it once that new nail has grown out to the
        tip. That is why the trial ran for 24 weeks, and why a one-month trial of anything for nails
        tells you nothing. More on timelines in <a href="/pages/how-long-does-collagen-take-to-work">how
        long collagen takes to work</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="jr-table-scroll">
        <table class="jr-table">
